-- title:
--   Complex exchange, signed network form
-- statement:
--   **Complex exchange, signed network form.** For any labelling, every gate is OK and the scalar circuit routes `w` to `ρ w` with sign `ε w`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.NetComplexLemma5`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NetComplex.complex_exchange_net {M : Type*} [AddGroup M] (hcard : ∀ t, #(ind t) = 3)
--       (hinj : Function.Injective ind) (lab : GName T → M) :
--       (∀ g ∈ cxGatesL R ind lab, g.OK) ∧
--         ∀ (v : Wr ind → R) w, scalarRun (cxGatesL R ind lab) v (NetComplex.ρ ind w) = NetComplex.ε R ind w * v w
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *Lemma 5 (complex construction) as a scalar gate network over a ring with `1/2`*: Scalars lie in a commutative ring `R` in which `2` is invertible (the paper uses `ℤ[i, 1/2]`).
--   Parameters as in `NetScalar`: a ground set `Fin h`, a finite type `T` of triples with
--   `ind : T → Finset (Fin h)`, `#(ind t) = 3`, `ind` injective.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** This lemma belongs to the Lean formalization (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign) of the OpenAI preprint *Integer multiplication below $n\log n$*: the array model of tape data (mixed-radix arrays and pull maps), the interchange networks of §3–4 (Propositions 7, 8, 11, Lemmas 9–12), the butterfly layers of §5 (Lemma 13, Proposition 14), the synthesis of §6–7 (Lemma 16, Proposition 18), the resampling and parameter choices of §8–9, and the final glue `IntMul.OpenAI.Glue.kappaBound_of_machine`, which derives the platform bound `KappaBound (1/2^182)` (from `Def_IntMul_MultitapeModel`) for any correct multitape machine meeting the paper's time recurrence. All names refer to the definition bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs1`–`IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs9`.
